<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3895" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλγ-έω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					12.27
				</span></i>
			, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλγος</span>) <i>feel bodily pain,
				suffer</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλγήσας</span>
			<i>smarting with pain</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.269
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>suffer, be ill</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.68
			</span></i>; more fully, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλγήσας ὀδύνῃσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					12.206
				</span></i>
			: suffering part in acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλγησον ἧπαρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					135
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς γνάθους ἀλγήσετε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pax</u>
					237
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν δάκτυλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					462d
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ὄμματα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				515e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>suffer hardship</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἢ ἁλὸς ἢ ἐπὶ
				γῆς ἀλγήσετε</span> Od.l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>feel pain of mind, grieve</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ.
				ψυχήν, φρένα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.43
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				608
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τινί</span>
			<i>to be pained at </i> a thing, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.120
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				744
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ ἐξειργασμένοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					377
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διά τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.68
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τι</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.65
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				240
			</span></i>: c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλγεῖν χρὴ τύχης παλιγκότου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					571
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				1256
			</span></i>: c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλγῶ μὲν ἔργα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					1016
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρᾶξιν ἢν ἤλγησ᾽ ἐγώ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					790
				</span></i>
			: c. part., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤλγησ᾽ ἀκούσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.50
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				844
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλγῶ κλύων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					86
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁρῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eup.
					117.2
				</span></i>
			 : abs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀλγοῦν</span>, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἡδόμενον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Sent.</u>
				4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποχόνδριον -ούμενον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Coac.</u>
					273
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ἀλγούμενον ὀδόντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					<u>Eup.</u>
					1.66
				</span></i>
			.</div>
